# /printpress — Drafting Workflow Skill

Full drafting pipeline. Genre-parameterized. The skill owns the cycle from data-in through save + learning loop. At Stage 3 it invokes `/critic-swarm` for adversarial review; revision and save remain inside /printpress.

This file is the executable workflow. Design rationale lives in `~/Documents/GitHub/cyborg-methodologies/printpress/SPEC.md`. Genre-specific logic lives in `genre_configs/[genre].md`. Interaction patterns (what the skill says at each stage) live in `UX_STUB.md`.

---

## When to use

Drafting any of:

- `academic_position` — academic faculty job applications (TT, VAP, lectureship, postdoc-in-academic-dept, open-rank). Reviewer = search committee. v1 ready.
- `grant_fellowship` — grants and fellowships with a review panel. v1 ready.
- `non_academic_application` — industry, tech, nonprofit, govt, EdTech, EA orgs. Reviewer = hiring manager + ATS.
- `peer_review` — journal articles, book chapters, manuscripts. ⚠️ Stage 1 not yet specified — do not run peer_review without a design conversation with the author (per SPEC § What's NOT in this spec yet).
- `other` — unknown genre. Skill asks the author; logs to learning loop for possible promotion.

**Standalone review (no drafting):** use `/critic-swarm` directly. /printpress is the drafting pipeline; /critic-swarm is the review-only door. See SPEC § Standalone review.

---

## Invocation

**/printpress is the orchestrator. The pipeline is decomposable; mid-cycle entry is supported.** Bare invocation reads working directory state to detect WHERE in the pipeline the work is, not just WHICH genre. Don't assume "/printpress means start from Stage 0." Detect first.

| Form | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `/printpress` | **State detection.** Read context (working dir, open files, recent conversation, existing artifacts). Determine: (a) which genre, (b) what stage the work is at. Confirm or offer continuation options. |
| `/printpress [genre]` | Explicit genre. Skips genre inference but still does state detection within that genre. |
| `/printpress draft [genre?]` | Force start from Stage 0. Use when the existing artifacts shouldn't drive the workflow (e.g., starting fresh on a new application). |
| `/printpress revise [draft-path]` | Stage 4 only. Existing draft + (optional) prior critic-swarm synthesis → sequential workshopping. |
| `/printpress qc [draft-path]` | Stage 4.5 only. Pre-save QC verification on a converged draft. |
| `/printpress check` | Stage 4.6 only. Requirements Compliance Gate: re-fetch the live posting/form, diff against the captured ledger, verify materials meet every structured requirement. Runnable standalone at any point, not just at readiness. |
| `/printpress save [draft-path]` | Stage 5 only. Mechanical cleanup, save final, append VERSION_LOG, voice-check learn pass. |

### State detection (bare invocation)

When invoked bare, **the skill reads the working directory and infers what stage the author is at** before assuming Stage 0:

| Working directory contains | Likely stage | Default offer |
|---|---|---|
| Just a `POSTING.md` (or nothing yet) | Stage 0 | "Start a new draft for [inferred genre]?" |
| `POSTING.md` + `DRAFT_PLAN.md`, no draft yet | Stage 2 (assembly) | "Draft the cold long-form assembly from the plan? (See Stage 2 assembly protocol.) Or revisit Stage 1?" |
| Workshopped prose exists but no cold assembly saved | Stage 2 (assembly capture) | "The opening was workshopped warm — dispatch a cold subagent to capture the independent assembly before we go further? (Protects the learning loop.)" |
| `*_ASSEMBLY_v0.md` present, no `ASSEMBLY_MARKS.md` | Stage 2 (author marking) | "Show the uncut assembly for keep / drop / unsure marking before any selection pass." |
| `*_ASSEMBLY_v0.md` + `ASSEMBLY_MARKS.md` present, no handoff draft | Stage 2 (selection experiment) | "Choose an inspectable cutting route: AI-proposed cut with diff, author-led selection with local AI compression, or hybrid." |
| `*_HANDOFF_v1.md` present, no `LEARNING_LOG.md` | Stage 3/4 | "Review the marked, post-selection handoff (critic-swarm or workshop)?" |
| Draft file present, no `LEARNING_LOG.md` | Stage 3 (review) | "Run critic-swarm on this draft? Or jump to Stage 4 revision?" |
| Draft + `LEARNING_LOG.md` (recent swarm output) | Stage 4 (revision) | "Workshop the synthesis flags? One at a time." |
| `*_final.md` exists, no recent VERSION_LOG entry | Stage 5 (save) | "Run mechanical cleanup + save + voice-check learn?" |
| Multiple drafts, mixed signals | Ambiguous | Ask the author what they want to do next. |

**Examples:**
- `/printpress` in a job application folder with just `POSTING.md` → infers `academic_position` from posting + Stage 0 → starts there.
- `/printpress` in a folder with a v3 draft and recent swarm output → recognizes mid-revision → "Pick up Stage 4 workshopping where we left off?"
- `/printpress grant_fellowship` from a folder with a finalized draft → state detection finds Stage 5 work pending → "Run save + voice-check learn?"
- `/printpress draft` from anywhere → forces Stage 0 even if other artifacts exist (use sparingly).

The orchestrator framing matters: /printpress conducts; voice-check, /critic-swarm, (eventually) /workshop do the work. Mid-cycle entry is the orchestrator picking up the baton wherever the author left it, not insisting on full-cycle execution.

