- **Requirements compliance is now a first-class gate, parallel to quality.** Prior design gated quality (Stage 4.5) but treated structured-requirement compliance as genre-buried and incidental — the recurring failure where materials are nearly done before a structured requirement (word cap, required statement, milestones/budget, portal field) surfaces. Fix is **upstream-weighted**: Stage 0 opens with a mandatory, cross-genre **Submission Requirements Ledger** (`APPLICATION_STRUCTURE.md`, universal) captured from the **live** posting + form. Every row receives an owner. `DRAFT` rows become Stage 1 allocation targets and Stage 2 hard constraints; `AUTHOR-HANDLED` and `PORTAL` rows remain in the compliance surface without becoming prose targets. Reference lists are always author-handled; academic CVs are author-handled; required résumés are drafted unless the author takes them over. Stage 4.6 re-fetches the live posting, diffs against the ledger, and blocks "ready" on any unmet/changed item (author can override explicitly). Runnable standalone via `/printpress check`.

